# Metal slab in a field under full Ewald with the finite-width charge SELF-ENERGY on the diagonal
# (`fix_modify gself`, 2026-08-23). Pins the term that lets a lattice-QEq metal screen like a
# conductor: without it this slab carries a staggered Nyquist mode (layer charges alternate at
# 2.2x the Gauss limit at the physical eta_Au and DIVERGE as eta->0); with it the response is
# monotone, Gauss to ~6%, and the eta->0 limit is a well-behaved conductor -- the behaviour of
# Scalfi et al.'s Thomas-Fermi electrode (JCP 153, 174704), whose Gaussian charges carry exactly
# this term implicitly. eta_Au = 5.172 is the physical TF hardness (l_TF = 0.72 A) and is NOT
# touched; the width 0.5 A is Scalfi's. PQEq (Gaussian) kernel, as the repo convention prefers.
# 240-atom orthorhombic Au(111), 5 layers, generated on-lattice (duplicate-free, checked).
units           metal
atom_style      full
boundary        p p f
read_data       data.au_ortho
pair_style      hybrid/overlay lj/cut 12.0 coul/long 12.0 coul/shield/intra 12.0 all gaussian
pair_coeff      * * lj/cut 0.0 1.0
pair_coeff      * * coul/long
pair_coeff      * * coul/shield/intra 1.618
kspace_style    pppm/samqeq 1.0e-6
kspace_modify   slab 3.0 mesh 24 28 80 gewald 0.35
neighbor        2.0 bin
set             atom 1 charge -0.01
set             atom 240 charge 0.01
fix             ef  all efield 0.0 0.0 0.5
fix             chg all qeq/sam 1 0.0 10.0 1.0e-8 au_pqeq.param
fix_modify      chg shield gaussian
fix_modify      chg gself on width 0.50
run             0
write_dump      all custom charges.dump id type q modify sort id format line "%d %d %.12g"
variable        peval equal pe
print           "${peval}" file pe.txt screen no
